leim is built separately from emacs, so src/emacs does not exist in this tree.
Makefile.in wants it for converting the TIT files and for byte-compiling, so
point it at the installed one instead.

	BUILT-EMACS = ${dot}${dot}/src/emacs
	  ->  ${LOCALBASE}/bin/emacs

That is what the dependency on emacs20 is for: it fixes the build order.

--- leim/Makefile.in.orig	Mon Jan 11 12:40:22 1999
+++ leim/Makefile.in	Tue Dec 28 14:53:29 1999
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 
 # Which Emacs to use to convert TIT files to Emacs Lisp files,
 # byte-compile Emacs Lisp files, and generate the file leim-list.el.
-BUILT-EMACS = ${dot}${dot}/src/emacs
+BUILT-EMACS = ${LOCALBASE}/bin/emacs
 
 buildlisppath=${srcdir}/${dot}${dot}/lisp
 
